"""Process all pending LLM-handoff JSON files generated by the Signal+Forager
pipeline and write `<file>.response.json` for each.

The hypothesis responses for the 5 high-value Command B batch candidates are
hand-authored by Claude Opus 4.7 (this file). They cite specific raw_items
the Forager actually retrieved during B v3 (after the seed_query bug fix on
2026-05-23) and are calibrated based on the real-world signal context.

For remaining handoffs (per-position F-monitor hypothesis, dossier_draft,
monitoring_draft), the script generates structured responses that match the
expected schema using lighter heuristics — explicitly flagged as
`generator: "template"` vs `generator: "claude-opus-4-7-inline"` so an
operator can later prioritise re-processing the template ones with deeper
reasoning if desired.

It also injects the high-value hypotheses back into the SQLite ForagerStore
so D/C re-runs would see them.

Usage:
    cd C:\\Signal\\bot && python process_llm_handoffs.py
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import json
import os
